  "scope": "Public constructors for pi, sqrt(2) and sin(1/3), minus independently directed dyadic floors at 80 and 1100 bits, with both signs and optional serialization reconstruction. Twenty-four sequential schedules check coarse zero-work reuse, finer misses and unlimited retry; 24 prewarmed eight-thread schedules reuse an actually spent shared allowance; 72 mixed eight-thread schedules combine shared small allowances, a separate large allowance and unlimited refinement. Six invalid-domain controls cover four threads each. Every successful sample encloses both 2560-bit directed MPFR endpoints, also rechecked using Python Fraction. Every definite fact agrees with the oracle and each thread retains all previously observed sign/zero/magnitude facts. Original serialization bytes must remain unchanged.",
  "limits": [
    "Caches and allowances are deliberately not serialized. A reconstructed root may initially answer Unknown; once that root is warmed its available facts must persist. Clone reuse shares the original root.",
    "The three scheduling offsets and yields are thread stress, not exhaustive interleavings or a formal concurrency proof.",
    "Query work counters are compared after joining, because separate concurrent getter calls need not form an atomic snapshot.",
    "All fixture construction and structural inspection remain outside explicit work allowances. No byte/time, globally cold-process, full-board or main-admission claim is made.",
    "This adds public coverage to an unchanged retained runtime. Existing private deterministic publication tests and the original capped cost failures remain separate evidence."
  ],
